Systematic fire safety work (SBA) is the ongoing process of keeping **fire safety** alive in an operation – not just a document in a binder.

## Parts of the work

- Risk assessment of fire hazards
- Routines for maintaining fire protection
- Training and drills for staff
- Documentation and follow-up

## The documentation must contain

1. Description of the operation
2. Fire compartments and escape routes
3. Control points and intervals
4. Division of responsibilities

### Evacuation

> Escape routes must be kept clear and signposted at all times, not just during inspections.

| Check | Interval |
| ----- | -------- |
| Escape routes | Continuous |
| Fire alarm | Per manufacturer |

